                                                "example_id": "76d809cf-57f2-48e6-ae5b-b1788892c373",
                                                "sense_id": "d1e07294-08d8-3cbf-927e-a47e951517be",
                                                "text": "I mind him well, and the burn we fished and the pickle things we took out, and your mother that played with us in her cutty sark, and not a shoe between us nor a bodle of money; but the green hills round us, and all we knew of the world that it lay beyond them."
